---
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="Print Your Quilt Project Plan"
  description="Print on desktop or export a print-ready PDF on phones and tablets with your complete quilt project plan."
  eyebrow="Learn QuiltClarity · Final step"
  guideSlug="print-your-project-plan"
  guideCategory="start_here"
  previous={{
    href: '/guides/read-your-cutting-plan/',
    label: 'Read Your Cutting Plan',
  }}
>
  <section>
    <h2>Recalculate before printing</h2><p>
      If the planner says Plan needs recalculation, select Recalculate first. On
      a phone or tablet, select export PDF for print, then open the downloaded
      file to print or save it. On desktop, select Print to open the browser
      print flow. The prepared date and optional project name identify the
      current output.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>What the printed plan includes</h2><p>
      The project status, shopping list, pattern comparison when used,
      assumptions, warnings, every stock allocation, purchased layout, cutting
      instructions and diagrams are included. Accessible text versions of
      allocations remain available on the planner page.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>What the printed plan omits</h2><p>
      Navigation, editing controls, help buttons, zoom controls, and screen-only
      actions are omitted. Diagrams use portrait or landscape pages according to
      their geometry and use grayscale-safe patterns.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Check before cutting</h2><p>
      Match the printed usable WOF, stock labels/dimensions, seam allowance,
      direction settings, and Buy now amount to your real project. Keep pattern
      instructions for construction order; QuiltClarity plans rectangular fabric
      cuts, not quilt assembly.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuidePage>
